# The script `mise run ffi-test` runs both ways, compared
# (tools/fixture-compare.sh; docs/dev-practices/headless-mode.md, "How the
# gate runs a fixture"), on the default set's editor over a real loop thread
# and on its fixture harness stepped (`fixture-test`), against
# the config in `config/`, to send keys with their identity as a window
# would. What it prints must be exactly `keys-expected`.

key a KeyA shift+control
key <Escape> Escape -
